rx36qkl678</link><guid isPermaLink="false">subsplash:2026-03-13T14:21:15.000-07:00</guid><pubDate>Fri, 13 Mar 2026 21:21:15 +0000</pubDate><description>This incident has been resolved.</description></item><item><title>Live Streaming Disruption [postmortem]</title><link>https://stspg.io/89zm3pjz4lcm</link><guid isPermaLink="false">subsplash:2026-03-08T06:53:52.363-07:00</guid><pubDate>Sun, 08 Mar 2026 13:53:52 +0000</pubDate><description>**Summary:**

A service disruption on March 8th impacted Subsplash Live performance and access to the Live section of the dashboard. During a period of high traffic, a rate limiting setting on our recently updated web gateway incorrectly flagged internal system traffic as an overload. This prevented some users from accessing their Subsplash Live accounts and caused a drop in livestream connection success rates.

**Timeline, Resolution &amp; Recovery:**

* Incident start: 6:00 AM PST
* Fix Applied: Our engineering team identified the bottleneck and disabled the restrictive setting at 7:30 AM PST, restoring full service by 7:38 AM PST.
* Video Backfill: All &quot;Live-to-On-Demand&quot; videos that were delayed during the outage have been successfully processed and are now visible in your library.

